[{:seon.task/name "no-clipping-functions"
  :seon.task/plan "Owner, 2026-10-21: \"no clipping functions, only general improvements to the one render function and custom render functions for both html and ai when we know that output needs to be improved for context.\" Lane RENDER; answers seon.fences/no-clip-in-renders (audit FENCES #47-49, its two proofs included here). Found: seon.render.ui/clip and /line (fixed character cuts with a bare …, used 24 times in seon.render.ui and 4 in seon.render.ai); bare top-N lists with no count of what they left (ui tile-tasks take 40 rows and take 8 attempts, tile-fx take 6 spent, tile-errors take-last 6, test-dots take 24, agent-card take-last 6 evals, ai section-work take 8 / take 5, section-costly take 5, section-events take 8, problems take-last 3 errors); seon.agent-proc's running form cut at 200 characters (agent_proc.clj:72,75) before it reaches root; seon.context/near's 30-character window. Replace each with: `seon.print/prose`, the one printer's face for text a person or a model reads as prose (a string shown unquoted under a token budget; a cut keeps whole lines and words where it can and says what it omitted, +N lines, +N chars, and how to read the rest when it has a source); every bounded list says how many more and where they are; the agent's running form travels whole. Delete clip and line. Also found and fixed: the stylesheet's own clips (text-overflow: ellipsis on forms, stream rows, the running form and branch; -webkit-line-clamp on the task; max-height with overflow hidden on printed values; a card hiding five of its six evaluations under a \"+N more\" that counted one), each replaced by the render's budget; the door's seon_context answered the block as an escaped string literal under the reply budget (entrance.clj :context, mcp.clj), now the text; the agent page's context was printed at 2,000 tokens while the model reads 16,000; root's context sized tokens at 4 chars while the printer sizes 3.2."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.print-test/prose-says-what-it-omitted
                      seon.render-test/no-cut-on-the-page-drops-silently
                      seon.render-test/root-context-names-what-each-list-left
                      seon.print-test/more-says-how-many-and-where
                      seon.print-test/a-one-line-cut-reads-the-source-rest
                      seon.render-test/the-page-says-what-it-keeps
                      seon.render-test/root-context-groups-blocked-tasks-by-what-blocks-them
                      seon.render-test/no-render-calls-clip
                      seon.render-test/a-capped-list-says-how-many-more}}
 {:seon.task/name "the-page-shows-only-what-acts"
  :seon.task/plan "Seen 2026-10-21 by lane RENDER's verifier on its own root: (1) an agent root stopped after its attempt ended keeps its card's merge, main, clone, interrupt and kill buttons (seon.render.ui/card-shell renders them once, at the card's first append, whatever the agent's state); (2) the health tile's steps/s for api, render and web read 2-4 steps/s with nothing happening: their own polling (render's tick, the web's sampling) is counted as work, a measurement that disturbs itself (AGENTS.md). Correct: an ended card's body carries its verbs (or the shell hides them by the body's state class); a proc's rate counts the steps that did work, its polls apart."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.render-test/an-ended-card-offers-no-live-verbs
                      seon.render-test/a-polling-proc-at-rest-reads-zero-work}}
 {:seon.task/name "an-attempt-row-shows-where-its-time-went"
  :seon.task/plan "Seen 2026-10-21 by lane RENDER's verifier: the attempts table shows a6's calc/neg attempt at 8,126 ms against its siblings' 100-250 ms, and nothing on the page says where the time went (seon.render.ui/attempt-row shows end-ms minus start-ms only). Lane AGENTS records each turn's split (:seon.turn/split: tests, context, model, eval, record; 7ef171b on jolt/agents). Once that is on main: the attempt row's ms cell shows the split summed over its turns (the largest part first, each part's ms), its title each turn's; the agent page's work box shows the split per turn. Replaces the bare span; no new measurement."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/needs #{"seon.turn/a-turn-records-what-it-saw-and-spent"}
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.render-test/an-attempt-row-shows-its-turns-split}}
 {:seon.task/name "one-owner-per-view-path"
  :seon.task/plan "Lane DUP-VIEWS (notes/duplicates-audit-2026-10-22.md, its DUP-VIEWS rows; owner, 2026-10-22: keep src small, resolve every duplicate path at its owner, no fences). Est. -120 src lines. One owner each, the copies deleted: (A1) the declared status sets: web's live?, the entrance's agents answer and the check harness read seon.root/gone-statuses; one properties reader, seon.contract/properties (seon.render/properties and seon.render.ui/config-panel's own reader delete), and contract/enum-values for the enums' members; seon.problems reads :seon.status/failed (added to :seon.attempt/status in seon.facts.edn) instead of #{:dead :lost}. (A11) root's view numbers (p50s, tx per commit, the windows dropped) are one pure fn, seon.root/view-numbers, which seon.root/state and seon.render.proc/system-value both call. (A12) a test run is red by seon.proofs/red?, read by the card's dots, the card's allowed line, the event's row and the proofs box. (A13) a card's evaluation row is history-row with a compact budget; an item's text is (or :printed :shown), the record keeping :shown for an error too (seon.repl/record-tx), not the error map read as text. (A14) a merge's result in words once (seon.render.ui/merge-words) for the card's pill and the event. (A15) my.root's create!/load-tasks!/load-docs! share one private write-declared!. (A18) the render proc's stats read seon.lib/summ. (A21) the web proc keeps its waiting pages and tabs with seon.step/pend and answered, not its own :next and :waiting. (B2) the second error shape {:error string} goes from the entrance (every refusal: :seon.root/refused; a defect: the thrown error map or :seon.root/proc-defect), ``seon.mcp/request!`` (an unreachable entrance; now bin/mcp's JSON-RPC error) and the web listener that cannot bind; the readers' (or (:seon.error/message r) (:error r)) patches in seon.render.proc, seon.render.ui and seon.root/start! delete. (B3) the zoom's {:status :unknown} and web's :bytes-per-s (a key nothing sets) delete. (B9) a root verb called from the page is recorded with its answer (the render proc records it when the answer arrives), not a fabricated \"requested\". (C5, C6) the fork server's standby row and the fx lanes line (numbers nobody reports) and seon.render.ai/tokens (an alias of seon.print.select/estimate) delete. (C9) seon.render.ui's doc cites seon.render/html. Producers of {:error string} outside this lane (root, agent, agent_proc) are reported to the root lane (DUP-ROOT), not fixed here."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.entrance-test/an-entrance-refusal-is-the-one-error-map
                      seon.web-test/a-root-verb-is-recorded-with-its-answer
                      seon.web-test/a-listener-that-cannot-bind-is-the-one-error-map
                      seon.render-test/a-recorded-error-shows-its-message
                      seon.render-test/a-refused-merge-says-why-once
                      seon.problems-test/a-lost-attempt-is-a-death}}
 {:seon.task/name "an-ended-agent-leaves-the-grid-by-an-event"
  :seon.task/plan "Found by lane HARVEST's clock census (bin/dragons clocks, docs/clocks.md#time-decides-owed-its-owners-fix). seon.render.proc/order leaves out an agent ended more than RETIRE-MS (90000, a literal, not config) ago, and seon.render.proc/ordered re-derives the order when the agents changed or a second passed (a literal 1000, a cache keyed by time): what the grid shows is decided by the clock, and an idle dashboard's content changes with nothing happening. v1: the grid showed live agents and the ended ones as their own section. Correct: an ended agent leaves the grid on an event (the next agent's start, the user's dismissal, or a bounded count of ended agents kept, each a config key), the order is derived when the agents changed and only then. Deletes RETIRE-MS, the :order-at clause and the :retire-ms caption field; the three leave docs/clocks.md's owed list."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.render-test/an-ended-agent-leaves-the-grid-by-an-event}}]
